  "steps": [
    "Rinse the lentils until the water runs clear, then add to a pot with the stock. Simmer for 20 minutes, skimming any foam, until collapsed and soft.",
    "While they cook, fry the onion in oil until soft, then add garlic, ginger and the whole spices. Cook until aromatic.",
    "Stir the spiced onion mixture into the lentils along with the coconut milk.",
    "Loosen with a little water if needed and simmer for a final 5 minutes.",
    "Season well and finish with fresh coriander and an optional tempering of sizzled mustard seeds."
  ],
  "notes": "For a tarka, sizzle extra mustard seeds and dried chilli in hot oil and pour over each bowl at the table — the drama is half the fun."
}
